        "id": 19099
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-08T15:10:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point, I agree it would logically make more sense for these to be logs instead of aborts. But generally, we often just get stack traces without logs, and then even when we do get logs, messages from our current `SkDebugf` logging function may not be present even when they should be. I\u0027ll send you a doc with more info / proposal to add more logging capabilities. However, Leon was suggesting we might want to add (temporary?) aborts here to try and pinpoint the current linked issue in the meantime, since sorting out logging design amongst the larger team might take some time.",
      "parentUuid": "0707c415_8ed64396",
      "revId": "cb4f1cc741ddc9ac312d0dabab1c15c31256b000",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "232e6a45_5603a061",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-08T15:17:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So since we do want to end up with logging in the long term, what if we set this up with a name that\u0027s more of a \"log\" type name. But in the short term Android can override this macro in their own config file to add an abort in. That way the idea of aborting stays out of the Skia code, but Android can still get their short term desires?",
      "parentUuid": "6223f466_95ecf443",
      "revId": "cb4f1cc741ddc9ac312d0dabab1c15c31256b000",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30c9ce7e_a6fd7523",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-08T15:48:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FWIW, this is similar to what we did in b/206415266, including https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/491977.\n\nI\u0027d be fine with putting \"LOG\" in the name, but I still think it needs to be clear that the intent is for it to be fatal (on Android). Otherwise it would be quite dangerous - if the same logging macro is used elsewhere only for the purposes of logging, a log that was never intended to be fatal anywhere becomes fatal on Android.\n\nI\u0027m not convinced we should use Android\u0027s name, but they have a macro of `LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL`. I\u0027d be fine with naming this something like `SK_LOG_OPTIONALLY_FATAL` (??). Somewhere else we could toggle whether these are fatal or not.",
      "parentUuid": "232e6a45_5603a061",
      "revId": "cb4f1cc741ddc9ac312d0dabab1c15c31256b000",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a6b808d_9b7720d0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-08T15:55:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess the issue is there is nothing fatal or abort worthy for Skia here. I\u0027d prefer to avoid have Androids interpretation of things leaking into Skia too much. Having a macro that\u0027s intended for Android\u0027s use only is okay (though not great, and hopefully skia revamped logging can fix that), but I\u0027m not a huge fan of how to handle the failure case leaking into Skia.",
      "parentUuid": "30c9ce7e_a6fd7523",
      "revId": "cb4f1cc741ddc9ac312d0dabab1c15c31256b000",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
