      "writtenOn": "2023-03-08T22:00:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess my concrete suggestions are:\n1) remove the word ABORT from the macro. Make the macro look more like a log statement inside of skia.\n2) Move the special Android defining of the macro out of SkAssert and instead define it inside Android itself in the SkUserConfig (or whatever the file is called). There Android can have the macro abort if it wants to.",
      "parentUuid": "127ef5fb_79401080",
